      "level": 2,
      "content": "EARLY NATIONALIST / MODERATE PHASE"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The period between 1885 and 1905 marks the Moderate or Early Nationalist Phase of the Indian National Movement.",
        "The formation of the Indian National Congress in 1885 created a single platform for national consciousness.",
        "Moderates employed constitutional methods, resolutions, petitions, and propaganda to push for governance reforms.",
        "Early nationalist leaders exposed the economic impact of British colonial rule through the Drain of Wealth Theory.",
        "Despite limitations in mass mobilization, this period laid the political and intellectual foundation for subsequent national struggles."
      ],
      "id": "1xwowvj"
